#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119580 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "38fce106-2ba8-554c-ace3-a5731d15a635" :question/math-academy-id "e-4949" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2)$. Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nPQ^(→) &= \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\mid comp_{n}PQ^(→) \\mid \\\\\n&= (\\begin{vmatrix}PQ^(→) \\cdot n &)/(\\mid n\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\\n&= (\\mid (-1) \\cdot 2 + 6 \\cdot 4 + 4 \\cdot (-4)\\begin{vmatrix})/(\\sqrt{2^{2} + 4^{2} + (-4)^{2}}) \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid - 2 + 24 - 16 \\mid}{\\sqrt{4 + 16 + 16}} \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 6\\end{vmatrix}}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119581 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "74693316-2e5a-5821-87a5-fdc5b8719c82" :question/math-academy-id "e-4950" :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,-2,-1)$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle = 4$, find the shortest distance from $P(0, -1, 2)$ to $\\Pi$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nPQ^(→) &= ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ - ⟨0,-1, 2⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1,-1,-3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\mid comp_{n}PQ^(→) \\mid \\\\\n&= (\\begin{vmatrix}PQ^(→) \\cdot n &)/(\\mid n\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\\n&= (\\mid 1 \\cdot 2 + (-1) \\cdot 0 + (-3) \\cdot (-2)\\begin{vmatrix})/(\\sqrt{2^{2} + 0^{2} + (-2)^{2}}) \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 2 + 0 + 6 \\mid}{\\sqrt{4 + 0 + 4}} \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 8\\end{vmatrix}}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{8} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119582 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1538dde4-ab62-502e-8efe-7f37628ab861" :question/math-academy-id "e-4951" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3, -10, 3)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $2x+y-2z = -1$." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z$. Let's choose $x=4$ and $y=-5$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + y - 2z &= -1 \\\\\n2(4) + (-5) + 1 &= 2z \\\\\n4 &= 2z \\\\\nz &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(4, -5, 2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nPQ^(→) &= ⟨4,-5, 2⟩ - ⟨3,-10, 3⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 5,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane\n\n$$\nax+by+cz=d\n$$\n\nthe normal vector is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\langle a,b,c \\rangle\n$$\n\nSo, for the plane $\\Pi$, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 1, -2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\mid comp_{n}PQ^(→) \\mid \\\\\n&= (\\begin{vmatrix}PQ^(→) \\cdot n &)/(\\mid n\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\\n&= (\\mid 1 \\cdot 2 + 5 \\cdot 1 + (-1) \\cdot (-2)\\begin{vmatrix})/(\\sqrt{2^{2} + 1^{2} + (-2)^{2}}) \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 2 + 5 + 2 \\mid}{\\sqrt{4 + 1 + 4}} \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 9\\end{vmatrix}}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a19b242a-113b-53c5-86a6-bfb730e43f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117625} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f9c813-a4c9-50c4-8468-85113fe94dab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117626} {:answer/id #uuid "b449447c-78be-5db3-8b6c-b9ab7dada1bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117627} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0d602a-a4f4-5de4-83d3-a9ba9d1a5098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117628} {:answer/id #uuid "0aa19295-68c2-5fd1-85dc-867efe60a782" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b449447c-78be-5db3-8b6c-b9ab7dada1bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117627} :answer-field/id #uuid "c556acd4-2606-5152-932e-27428090cf80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117624}] :question/id #uuid "7f22d111-9bd0-53c0-9506-a867aa25de4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33466" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3, 5,-2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r - \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} = 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abd36b49-5d8e-5b12-8ab6-c2e5ca34de99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117851} {:answer/id #uuid "cc29e69a-9917-538e-8d66-c249d223dd2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26\\sqrt{17}}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117852} {:answer/id #uuid "d1728ea2-cab7-5cb4-b648-355dbc425c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117853} {:answer/id #uuid "fc6e5299-5544-5b48-9806-18b3d57ba0a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19\\sqrt{17}}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117854} {:answer/id #uuid "3e41c289-4b70-52e3-abc6-d64fb28bc369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23\\sqrt{17}}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc29e69a-9917-538e-8d66-c249d223dd2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26\\sqrt{17}}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117852} :answer-field/id #uuid "f961e607-2db0-5314-894f-2fa4ec2daf5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117850}] :question/id #uuid "6fe2eafb-89b6-55ce-bbec-c86f82bc889c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34031" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1, 2,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r - ⟨1,-5, 3⟩) \\cdot ⟨1, 0, 4⟩ = 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b17a8e9-e121-520f-9807-60528270590a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117881} {:answer/id #uuid "9a37a2b6-1e22-5ed8-bdd7-06268010dfff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117882} {:answer/id #uuid "ecea184a-a116-5d83-88d5-9e198b901a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117883} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f0e9d4-8634-59e0-b3b2-251ea5758aeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117884} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbcff2d-c54a-5e05-841b-c57bfe8afe74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{26}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a37a2b6-1e22-5ed8-bdd7-06268010dfff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117882} :answer-field/id #uuid "f492f940-e7fb-514a-9944-bc176a5024c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117880}] :question/id #uuid "c2558d4d-1eea-5e1f-b2f5-44cc93092823" :question/math-academy-id "q-34075" :question/problem "Given that $Q(1, 3, 5)$ lies on the plane $Π: r \\cdot ⟨ - 4, 1,-3⟩ =-16$, find the shortest distance from $P(-3, 7, 3)$ to $Π$."}]}
